@104 = ~Unicorn Grove
We destroyed the core within the memories and, with it, the shard itself. The dark magic that had taken hold of Unicorn Grove should gradually fade, freeing the unicorns from its influence.~

@300 = ~...~
@301 = ~I'm glad we could bring an end to the shard's influence. You are always welcome here.~
@302 = ~That's understandable. Take it easy. What was it like inside? Did you see any pleasant memories?~
@303 = ~It did. You have done more for us than I could ever repay.~
@304 = ~You woke up! Here, take it easy. You might feel a little drowsy for a few minutes. Sit down.~
@305 = ~It'd better've been worth it to risk our bloody hides for a blasted herd of horn-horses!~
@306 = ~The shard exploded into pieces moments before you awoke. You destroyed the core, didn't you? How do you feel?~
@307 = ~Like I've been to the Nine Hells and back.~
@308 = ~Are the unicorns going to be all right?~
@309 = ~How do you think I feel? This had better pay off in the end.~
@310 = ~Tell me what you remember, if you feel able to speak of it.~
@311 = ~Nothing pleasant about it.~
@312 = ~A fine way to ruin one's memories. That's all I'll say.~
@313 = ~I survived. That's all that matters.~
@314 = ~Yes. According to Emhrys, the dark energy inhabiting the grove will dissipate over the next few hours. With the shard destroyed, there should be no further trouble.~
@315 = ~The unicorns had better be grateful for this ordeal, because I'm never doing it again.~
@316 = ~Trust me. They are.~
@317 = ~I'll take your word for it. I am in your debt. For everything you've done for me and the grove, you deserve a reward worthy of your courage. Here, please accept 8,000 gold coins as a token of my gratitude. I wish I could offer more, but I hope it will suffice. You will always be welcome at Unicorn Grove.~
@318 = ~The pleasure is ours, Eaglehorn. I'm glad we resolved this matter, however painful those memories were for some of us.~
@319 = ~Another good deed to our credit. I hope it makes up in some small way for the nightmares you endured, <CHARNAME>.~
@320 = ~May Shar never again demand that I aid creatures of the light. It leaves a distaste in my mouth.~
@321 = ~Safe travels, and good luck with whatever trials await you next.~
@322 = ~I'm glad to see you alive and well. May Silvanus always guide your way.~
